			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1577547">
									

<p>I feel that citation is overused here in some places. &quot; &quot;I don't remember doing that,&quot; was a frequent response to reminders of previously committed crimes or known family histories; equally frequent was the insistence, &quot;you asked me here to talk about the family&quot;. &quot; is the most egregious. It breaks the tone somewhat.</p>
<p>The rest of the article is not good enough for an upvote too, partly because we already have two skips with similar effects (<a href="/scp-1500">1500</a> and <a href="/scp-091">091</a>), and partly because there is nothing interesting revealed about the Bonifay Family itself. Some hints about what they did and how they lived, and maybe how that caused the creation of 1890, would be a nice way to make the article more interesting. Maybe list the details consistent between all recollections.</p>
<p>The fact that the album have different number of pages, photos move, and there is no way to figure out which caption refers to who, is very neat.</p>

